WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:03.280
We, the Windermere Kingdom,

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:07.520
have figured out how to mind control the 
Var-infected with the song of the wind.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:11.340
By unleashing the power of the ruins, we were able to establish the Starwind sector.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:14.700
Seven years have passed since our war of independence.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:21.020
The years took their toll on King Gramia. His wind weakened and his rune fell dark.

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:24.870
Compared to Earthlings, our time is short.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:30.800
Why can they live so much longer 
than the other humanoid races?

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.710
They are weak and runeless. It's unfair.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:40.780
Our lives are so short.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.060
Very soon, the runes of those on the frontlines shall fall dark as well.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:53.950
Analyzing the heritage of the Protoculture is crucial for us to break free from the chains of our fate.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:01:00.190
We shall bring the song of the 
great wind to the entire galaxy!

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:06.940
<i>Our kiss will send us leaping to the edge of space</i>

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:11.370
<i>Our affection is too hot for mere passionate love</i>

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:16.220
<i>We can be in absolute zero</i>

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:31.020
<i>I'll spark a dream in you</i>

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:35.540
<i>I'll embrace all you believe in</i>

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.160
<i>Let your genes go wild</i>

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:45.040
<i>I love you so much, but I try to play it cool sometimes</i>

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.890
<i>Tear off my mask and squeeze me to a whole new dimension</i>

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:55.860
<i>By banging into each other, we confirm our uncovered love</i>

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:00.260
<i>The tears we can't cry on our own connect us to the future</i>

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.880
<i>Our passionate love will shoot us into a super nova-like state</i>

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:12.770
<i>We can do this! No wounds can hold us back if we're together</i>

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.490
<i>Show me your passion, pray to the skies</i>

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.860
<i>Our super big bang will breathe life into a new genesis</i>

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.120
<i>We burn our lives for this fusion</i>

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:27.600
<i>We are in absolute zero</i>

00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:35.760
Planet Windermere

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.700
There are so many Draken IIIs.

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.110
I just hope they won't get in our way.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:59.490
We finally get to thrust our blade into the very heart of the UN Government.

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.560
Hold the fort for us, all of you.

00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.200
Da!

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.740
Cassim.

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:09.870
I know.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:14.950
Defeat the UN Government and 
establish the great galactic civilization.

00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:18.480
It's the last will of the late King Gramia.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.220
Note that only Roid heard him, though.

00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:30.730
<i>Ride on... Three, two, one</i>

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.440
<i>Stars, people, and apples are all the same</i>

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:41.610
<i>We're all pores and particles in the end</i>

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:45.400
<i>Pop sha' wo' pop sha' wa sha' yeah</i>

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:51.290
<i>We may be part of laws and rhythm,</i>

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:53.540
<i>but if we break—</i>

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.960
Is entering without permission what passes for good manners in Epsilon?

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.680
Freyja Wion and Mikumo Guynemer.

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.990
I've had my eyes on those two as well.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:12.710
However, Windermere has King Heinz, the Wind Singer.

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.480
Why are you interested in them?

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.940
Are you so surprised I would research my enemies?

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:21.370
I see.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.950
Oh, I forgot!

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:29.160
With the arrival of the six-unit SV-262 platoon,

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.910
the second expansion project is now complete.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:36.880
Once we are finished analyzing the Protoculture's heritage,

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:39.860
please do provide us with field data.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.590
Infiltrating Voldor?!

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:48.060
Yes. Unless we deal with those giant structures,

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:51.390
we can't even start thinking about turning the tables on Windermere.

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:56.910
Other than that they can echo a 
song's fold waves across the galaxy,

00:04:56.910 --> 00:04:59.150
the truth is that we know nothing about them.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.530
Gotta get close to figure it out!

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.300
We'll return to that planet once more.

00:05:13.100 --> 00:05:15.920
Back at it again at Cat Planet.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.330
Right...

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:21.100
Have you been sick or something?

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:21.840
What's the plan?

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:27.440
Land on Voldor, infiltrate the giant structure,

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:31.180
get it to react to Walküre's songs, and collect the data.

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.770
But why Voldor?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:36.480
We've got insider help.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:41.900
A surviving NUNS unit is continuing 
resistance in hopes of liberating Voldor.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:44.860
They've become immunized due to our songs.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:49.280
There's not many of them, but it seems like they can withstand the song of the wind.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:56.040
According to them, the Windermereans are withdrawing their garrison.

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.340
I figure they need them more elsewhere.

00:05:59.340 --> 00:06:02.250
Their frontline is drawn long and thin.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:05.970
We're going to take advantage of their shortage of men.

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:07.950
What about the other half of the plan?

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:11.720
We've infiltrated once already, so they must've tightened up security.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:14.930
Yeah, it's not gonna go as smoothly this time.

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:16.480
But worry not...

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:26.280
What's going on?

00:06:26.590 --> 00:06:27.800
Look at that!

00:06:34.820 --> 00:06:39.960
<i>Welcome to Walküre world</i>

00:06:37.490 --> 00:06:39.960
To everyone watching the galactic network!

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:44.330
The globular cluster is under Windermerean control,

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:48.900
and we, Walküre, can't travel around to perform anti-Var Waccine shows.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.140
<i>Welcome!</i>

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:54.060
<i>My Heart... feel your Love</i>

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.350
But we can't just sit idly.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.020
So we'll perform a special show

00:06:54.890 --> 00:07:01.370
<i>Welcome to Walkure World</i>

00:06:56.020 --> 00:06:58.980
and broadcast it across the galaxy!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:04.670
To everyone across all the stars and nations of the universe, we want to inspire you!

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.010
We're here to prove to Windermere that no matter what happens,

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.200
we'll never give up!

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:18.750
Let the songs of a goddess ring through the galaxy!

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:27.840
<i>Switch into gear! Screaming! No stopping now</i>

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:31.190
<i>S.O.S. the sirens are howling</i>

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:34.640
<i>Love's halation THE WAR</i>

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:39.650
<i>My own story begins as I wake up</i>

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:41.350
This broadcast carries a virus specially made by Reina.

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:46.010
<i>This morning feels different. I rub my eyes</i>

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.290
Virus?

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:43.850
Yep.

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:52.570
It's designed to infect all devices connected to the galactic network in the globular cluster.

00:07:46.010 --> 00:07:47.940
<i>Ready to fire! Three, two</i>

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.150
<i>onepiece flying as I spin</i>

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:55.440
<i>My engine is now in extreme speed</i>

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:59.370
It then multiplies exponentially and continues to spread.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.720
<i>Then we crash and a galactic level</i>

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.750
<i>Boom comes for your deculture!</i>

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:07.350
<i>All power starboard! I'm setting you on fire</i>

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:10.170
So we're making the enemy focus all their attention on Walküre?

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:13.150
<i>Feel it? Diving! There's no turning back</i>

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:13.970
The best place to hide a jellyfish is inside a bloom of them.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:16.490
<i>S.O.S. the signal's on fire</i>

00:08:14.350 --> 00:08:16.100
Isn't that kinda going too far?

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:19.220
Oh, we haven't even gotten to the good part yet.

00:08:16.490 --> 00:08:19.220
<i>Love's changing THE WORLD</i>

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:21.730
Let's click!

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:25.290
Thanks for watching!

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.730
This is a little something from me to you!

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:35.070
<i>We're surrounded by colors all around</i>

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.490
My dickulture!

00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:44.670
Not only are we breaking through their security, we are also making serious money at the same time.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:47.290
I applaud your ingenuity.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:51.260
<i>Hello</i>

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.180
The progress on the virus?

00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:00.010
32% of the network has been infected and it's still growing.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:57.340
<i>Hello</i>

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:02.770
<i>Hip and hop as the clock ticks and tocks</i>

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.850
<i>Restlessly flutter around like a butterfly</i>

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:11.820
<i>Don't stare at me so impatiently</i>

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:17.800
<i>I'm so tired, glittering with— oh give me a break!</i>

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:15.820
Your singing has changed.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:24.870
<i>Tingle-tingle? Something's wrong... My heart's out of control</i>

00:09:18.430 --> 00:09:19.330
Was it him?

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:27.290
Oh, uh, but your singing is different too, Mikumo.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:30.870
<i>Thimpety thump, it won't stop. No one told me about this!</i>

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:29.520
Has it?

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.340
How?

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:36.750
<i>Feelings rolling all around the clock</i>

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:36.300
Well... It used to be sparkly and rainbowy...

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:38.330
Now it's more...

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:39.710
<i>I'm so awkward when I'm around you</i>

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.470
Not as sparkly?

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.850
That's not what I meant.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:42.560
<i>I feel like I'm some bugged robot</i>

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:42.460
How should I put it?

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:48.100
It's still sparkly, but it's also like, fluffy and stuff now.

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:45.610
<i>Please just ignore me, this doesn't count</i>

00:09:45.610 --> 00:09:53.230
<i>I'm just tingling all over, walking the edge</i>

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.120
Something's wrong with Mikumo.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:00.910
Something's off.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.750
<i>Nobody ever celebrated your birthdays?</i>

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.790
<i>Not just that.</i>

00:10:09.790 --> 00:10:12.960
<i>I don't remember my parents or where I was raised.</i>

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:18.550
<i>All I have is an urge to sing. That's it.</i>

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:21.390
<i>Mikumo, are you—</i>

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.890
<i>Who needs a past?</i>

00:10:24.780 --> 00:10:27.800
<i>All that matters is that I get to sing in the present.</i>

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.020
<i>Are you ready?</i>

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>I heard a rumor that the world's gonna end someday</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:57.420
<i>Just kidding, it's obviously a lie</i>

00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:02.090
<i>I remember looking up at the sky</i>

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:06.100
<i>and feeling like I was in the future</i>

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:03.850
Freyja...

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:11.900
<i>I felt completely in sync with your wind</i>

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:14.940
Freyja's making her rune shine too much.

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.980
<i>You make me truly feel like a girl</i>

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:20.070
Who can blame her after receiving a present like that from Haya-Haya?

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:28.370
<i>so I've got no choice but to do it. I can't stop now!</i>

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:29.790
<i>You better be ready!</i>

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:33.130
<i>If my rune shines with a flash</i>

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:37.000
<i>wow woh wow woh</i>

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.420
<i>I fall in love</i>

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:43.260
<i>wow wow wow woh...</i>

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:49.960
<i>Lalali lalala you make me</i>

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:47.770
What's wrong?

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:49.540
Nothing...

00:11:49.540 --> 00:11:52.830
Come on, man. Did their music get you too?

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>Lalala rune pika invincible</i>

00:11:52.830 --> 00:11:54.150
Dude, please.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:19.840
<i>My eyes are tearing up with new excitement, alas, a tear drops</i>

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:26.880
<i>Come and knock on my heartbroken door</i>

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:35.020
<i>You're part of the tear that just dropped too</i>

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:41.730
<i>Hug me, eat me, make me sugarless please</i>

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:38.470
Thanksies.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:44.980
What did you think of my song, Hayate?

00:12:42.990 --> 00:12:49.480
<i>The dreams that girls have</i>

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:50.170
Mikumo told me my singing's changed.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:50.910
It sure has!

00:12:50.350 --> 00:12:57.890
<i>are a bit unreasonable to boys</i>

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:58.920
Before you'd take off slowly then go up and swoosh!

00:12:57.890 --> 00:13:04.270
<i>The true kiss we shared</i>

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:03.780
But today it was as if I was really flying in the sky.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:06.050
It was amazing. It literally blew me away.

00:13:05.200 --> 00:13:11.620
<i>was a short and sweet moment</i>

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.680
As awesome as it gets!

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:17.650
My chest feels tight all of a sudden...

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:19.920
<i>I'll give you an A for your meltingly sweet love</i>

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:26.990
<i>Come get another mouthful into my world of love</i>

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:34.740
<i>My eyes are tearing up with new excitement, alas, a tear drops</i>

00:13:29.260 --> 00:13:35.910
My heart's been racing ever since...

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:41.600
<i>Come and knock on my heartbroken door</i>

00:13:42.400 --> 00:13:49.860
<i>You're part of the tear that just dropped too</i>

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:56.700
<i>Hug me, eat me, make me sugarless please</i>

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.660
Hayate...

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.150
You know, I...

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:01.110
Freyja!

00:14:01.530 --> 00:14:04.610
You were amazing on stage tonight!

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.280
Thank you very much!

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.680
Keep it up! Good luck!

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.590
We're all behind you!

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:13.660
Let's go.

00:14:13.660 --> 00:14:14.240
Yeah.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:24.670
You know, the first time I saw 
people with wrinkles was on Ragna.

00:14:26.470 --> 00:14:30.090
Windermereans don't get wrinkles.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:37.480
At first I thought they were Wrinklians from another planet or something.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.440
I see.

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:41.980
I guess they've been together very long.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:42.900
Yeah.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:50.430
They must've made a lot of fun 
and happy memories together.

00:14:50.430 --> 00:14:51.360
Yeah.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:56.600
That reminds me, I haven't been home in ages.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:59.070
I haven't seen my mom in a long time.

00:14:59.070 --> 00:15:02.250
I did tell her I was going to Ragna, though.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:04.350
You should go back every now and then.

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:06.030
She's family.

00:15:06.030 --> 00:15:08.160
It's no big deal.

00:15:08.160 --> 00:15:09.380
It's just a couple of years.

00:15:15.610 --> 00:15:24.680
<i>I'm the kind of girl who'd challenge herself to take off into space</i>

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.730
Let's go out with a bang!

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:31.570
<i>There are a lot of sounds you don't know in this world</i>

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:37.160
<i>Many melodies you don't know in this dark flight</i>

00:15:37.160 --> 00:15:43.290
<i>Amidst this chaos, there's something out there</i>

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:46.590
<i>that hides extremely painful love...</i>

00:15:44.470 --> 00:15:46.090
What the hell are you all doing?

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.300
Sir Bogue!

00:15:48.300 --> 00:15:50.370
How fucking dare you?!

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.580
This isn't what it looks like!

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:53.510
We're learning about the enemy!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:54.970
Learning about?!

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:57.220
This is enemy propaganda!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:59.730
<i>In this story</i>

00:15:59.730 --> 00:16:06.260
<i>A copy of you comes out</i>

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.300
How do you turn this off?!

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:10.310
<i>Should I try to agitate you?</i>

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:12.470
<i>Should I threaten you?</i>

00:16:10.650 --> 00:16:11.740
You're worthless.

00:16:12.470 --> 00:16:15.940
<i>Now, do as you please,</i>

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:17.190
I'm not a cheap woman.

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:18.210
<i>and penetrate me</i>

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.930
Not showing you anything for so little!

00:16:18.210 --> 00:16:22.030
<i>Should we give a chance</i>

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:24.020
<i>to our love?</i>

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.380
Fuck you, Walküre!

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:27.630
<i>Quick, before the timer alarm</i>

00:16:27.630 --> 00:16:33.920
<i>goes off loudly and clearly</i>

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.130
Infection rate: 100%!

00:16:33.790 --> 00:16:37.220
We've got reports of significant 
transmission troubles in the cluster.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:38.600
The operation was a success!

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.370
We did it!

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:47.230
Heck yeah, Walküre!

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:50.650
All right!

00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:52.450
Launch the Aether!

00:16:52.450 --> 00:16:53.430
Roger!

00:16:58.490 --> 00:16:59.910
Are you sortieing?

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:01.630
Yes.

00:17:01.630 --> 00:17:03.780
Have you recovered?

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:04.780
Yeah.

00:17:04.780 --> 00:17:06.060
Good to hear.

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.130
When you have the time, please tell me about my da—

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.130
Leave here right away.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.290
You're still young.

00:17:15.290 --> 00:17:17.800
You don't have to suffer.

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:20.220
What are you talking about?

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:23.400
You of all must not face Windermere.

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:26.060
Why do you bring up Windermere?

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:37.360
You're late! We're ab—

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.450
What the fuck is going on?!

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:41.870
Why mustn't I get involved with Windermere?!

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.040
You, Major Kino, and my dad 
were on Windermere, I figure?

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:51.670
Did he tell you?

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:54.010
What's the deal with my dad?

00:17:55.180 --> 00:17:56.380
Girls.

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:57.380
It's okay.

00:17:58.540 --> 00:18:00.310
He would've found out eventually.

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.440
Wright Immelmann dropped the 
dimensional weapon on Windermere.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.650
Your father did.

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:14.320
No way.

00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:20.520
It was seven years ago, in the final days of Windermere's war of independence.

00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:26.960
NUNS 77th Air Wing, Major Wright Immelmann

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:30.670
contacted the Windermerean 
independence fighters in secret

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:35.140
and stole a dimensional warhead that the 
forces didn't even officially have on paper.

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:37.120
Then...

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:45.220
He annihilated the NUNS forces along with their entire garrison base

00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:49.450
and a great number of local civilians.

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:51.960
No way...

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:06.500
So the Windermerean version was true, then?

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:10.620
Why would NUNS lie in the first place?

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:14.120
Treaties forbid not only the use of dimensional weapons,

00:19:14.120 --> 00:19:17.800
but also the transportation of them to planets.

00:19:17.800 --> 00:19:20.720
NUNS broke those treaties.

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:23.560
Why?

00:19:23.560 --> 00:19:25.890
Why have you kept me in the dark?!

00:19:25.890 --> 00:19:28.350
Because it's military top secret.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:29.800
Satisfied now?

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:33.440
Let's move on with the briefing now.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.980
Worried about Hayate?

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:44.000
Or shocked by the NUNS lie?

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:49.240
When you get to be as big as the NUNS is, you're bound to get some nasty bits.

00:19:49.240 --> 00:19:52.980
I figure that's what the Windermereans hated.

00:19:53.860 --> 00:19:56.490
Ragna's a colony too, so I get it.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:20:00.400
There's plenty to get pissed about the UN Government.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.040
I mean, they're people from another planet.

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:08.000
But if you ask me, you just gotta let it slide.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:10.180
Nothing's worth more than peace.

00:20:11.540 --> 00:20:14.000
I guess Windermere couldn't do that.

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:18.650
People who do put their whole heart into things can get pretty scary when they're angered.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:32.940
Captain Wright, your father, was a real oddball.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:35.930
He'd collect absolutely ordinary rocks,

00:20:35.930 --> 00:20:38.690
get attached to completely useless junk,

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:41.090
and just acted in a way that left you scratching your head.

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:45.750
He'd gather Windermerean kids and play with them.

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.460
I guess that was because they reminded him of you.

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.780
I don't know what the truth is,

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:58.270
but I believe he wasn't the kind to commit a senseless genocide.

00:20:59.950 --> 00:21:03.110
What do you think, Hayate Immelmann?

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:05.770
Mission 17: Scatter on Stage

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.970
<i>I stand on the burning wreckage</i>

00:21:28.970 --> 00:21:35.690
<i>I don't know for how long or why at all</i>

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:40.450
<i>The flames around are drowning me</i>

00:21:40.450 --> 00:21:46.950
<i>Finding what I seek feels so pointless now</i>

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:52.700
<i>Break the world and go beyond the ecstasy of the past</i>

00:21:52.700 --> 00:21:59.080
<i>Choose the future even if it's the inferior option</i>

00:21:59.080 --> 00:22:00.040
<i>Let's go</i>

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:03.050
<i>Love forever until the very end</i>

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:05.970
<i>Sing so hard until it hurts</i>

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:11.760
<i>Until your soul finally settles down</i>

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:14.670
<i>But if you still want to sing then</i>

00:22:14.670 --> 00:22:17.500
<i>If you want to bet all on living</i>

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:23.320
<i>The purity of your heart will destroy everything</i>

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:28.270
<i>Ah, believe in me, baby</i>

00:22:28.270 --> 00:22:35.000
<i>I'll forgive you in a chaotic climax</i>

00:22:47.860 --> 00:22:49.970
We've already secured a landing route.

00:22:50.490 --> 00:22:53.350
Thank you for your help, Captain Larrazabal.

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:56.890
Hurry! We've got no time to waste!

00:22:56.890 --> 00:22:59.140
All Delta Platoon units locked in!

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:02.650
Hayate?

00:23:02.650 --> 00:23:04.090
I know.

00:23:05.190 --> 00:23:07.450
Figuring stuff out can wait.

00:23:07.450 --> 00:23:09.860
I've got my own job to worry about right now.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:17.410
I'll see the truth for myself one day.

00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:21.210
Hayate...

00:23:22.310 --> 00:23:26.330
If you ever require my assistance, just say the word.

00:23:27.650 --> 00:23:28.780
Thanks.

00:23:32.610 --> 00:23:34.300
Commence operation!

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.720
Infiltrating Voldor!

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:39.810
Next time: Sense Emergence
